<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><?xml-stylesheet href="/pretty-feed-v3.xsl" type="text/xsl"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Podcatcher on Hugo van Kemenade</title><link>https://hugovk.dev/tags/podcatcher/</link><description>Recent content in Podcatcher on Hugo van Kemenade</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en</language><copyright>&lt;a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/"&gt;{{&lt; icon "cc" &gt;}}&amp;hairsp;{{&lt; icon "cc-by" &gt;}}&amp;hairsp;{{&lt; icon "cc-sa" &gt;}}&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;Hugo van Kemenade&lt;br&gt;&lt;p class="text-xs text-neutral-500 dark:text-neutral-400"&gt;Powered by &lt;a class="hover:underline hover:decoration-primary-400 hover:text-primary-500" href="https://gohugo.io/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Hugo&lt;/a&gt; &amp;amp; &lt;a class="hover:underline hover:decoration-primary-400 hover:text-primary-500" href="https://github.com/jpanther/congo" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Congo&lt;/a&gt; &amp;amp; &lt;a class="hover:underline hover:decoration-primary-400 hover:text-primary-500" href="https://hugovk.dev" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Hugo&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</copyright><lastBuildDate>Thu, 08 Sep 2011 22:47:38 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://hugovk.dev/tags/podcatcher/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Symbian platform share in the Ovi Store (II)</title><link>https://hugovk.dev/blog/2011/symbian-platform-share-ii/</link><pubDate>Thu, 08 Sep 2011 22:47:38 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://hugovk.dev/blog/2011/symbian-platform-share-ii/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Here are some charts generated by &lt;a href="../symbian-platform-share"&gt;Ovid&lt;/a&gt; showing the Symbian&#10;platform share for some applications in Ovi Store.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;First up,&#10;&lt;a href="https://web.archive.org/web/20110930083815/http://code.google.com/p/mobbler/"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mobbler&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&#10;with 100,000 Ovi Store downloads (21st February - 31st Augst 2011):&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;figure&gt;&#10; &#10; &#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10; &#10; &lt;picture&#10; class="mx-auto my-0 rounded-md"&#10; &#10; &gt;&#10; &#10; &#10; &#10; &#10; &lt;source&#10; &#10; srcset="https://hugovk.dev/blog/2011/symbian-platform-share-ii/ovid-mobbler-2011-08_hu_e007ea4cbba16ac0.webp 330w,https://hugovk.dev/blog/2011/symbian-platform-share-ii/ovid-mobbler-2011-08_hu_a9355dc720e4a335.webp 660w&#10; &#10; &#10; ,https://hugovk.dev/blog/2011/symbian-platform-share-ii/ovid-mobbler-2011-08_hu_86e4026f0dbcee48.webp 1024w&#10; &#10; &#10; &#10; &#10; ,https://hugovk.dev/blog/2011/symbian-platform-share-ii/ovid-mobbler-2011-08_hu_86e4026f0dbcee48.webp 1024w&#10; &#10; "&#10; &#10; sizes="100vw"&#10; type="image/webp"&#10; /&gt;&#10; &#10; &lt;img&#10; width="1024"&#10; height="600"&#10; class="mx-auto my-0 rounded-md"&#10; alt="Mobbler"&#10; loading="lazy" decoding="async"&#10; &#10; src="https://hugovk.dev/blog/2011/symbian-platform-share-ii/ovid-mobbler-2011-08_hu_ade316448f7e47d2.png" srcset="https://hugovk.dev/blog/2011/symbian-platform-share-ii/ovid-mobbler-2011-08_hu_8055fccefbd8d41f.png 330w,https://hugovk.dev/blog/2011/symbian-platform-share-ii/ovid-mobbler-2011-08_hu_ade316448f7e47d2.png 660w&#10; &#10; ,https://hugovk.dev/blog/2011/symbian-platform-share-ii/ovid-mobbler-2011-08.png 1024w&#10; &#10; &#10; ,https://hugovk.dev/blog/2011/symbian-platform-share-ii/ovid-mobbler-2011-08.png 1024w&#10; "&#10; sizes="100vw"&#10; &#10; /&gt;&#10; &lt;/picture&gt;&#10; &#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;/figure&gt;&#10;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;The ratio of touch/non-touch decreased but then increased from 65/35 to 55/45. The&#10;initial large 25% share of Symbian^3 is explained by the fact that the Ovi Store release&#10;was the first to support S^3. This quickly decreased to the S^3 store average of 15%.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;I&amp;rsquo;ve also updated the Ovid script to include Symbian Anna and Belle devices too, and you&#10;can just see a tiny Anna sliver sneaking in along the bottom. Belle also has some Nokia&#10;700 and 701 downloads, but it&amp;rsquo;s too small to show up.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;hr&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Next up,&#10;&lt;a href="https://web.archive.org/web/20110921195226/http://projects.developer.nokia.com/podcatcher"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Podcatcher&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&#10;(February - May 2011):&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;figure&gt;&#10; &#10; &#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10; &#10; &lt;picture&#10; class="mx-auto my-0 rounded-md"&#10; &#10; &gt;&#10; &#10; &#10; &#10; &#10; &lt;source&#10; &#10; srcset="https://hugovk.dev/blog/2011/symbian-platform-share-ii/ovid-podcatcher-201102-201105_hu_d4ff1683b62ffac5.webp 330w,https://hugovk.dev/blog/2011/symbian-platform-share-ii/ovid-podcatcher-201102-201105_hu_f2087f2d389b0982.webp 660w&#10; &#10; &#10; ,https://hugovk.dev/blog/2011/symbian-platform-share-ii/ovid-podcatcher-201102-201105_hu_93ed9cfd29da89bb.webp 800w&#10; &#10; &#10; &#10; &#10; ,https://hugovk.dev/blog/2011/symbian-platform-share-ii/ovid-podcatcher-201102-201105_hu_93ed9cfd29da89bb.webp 800w&#10; &#10; "&#10; &#10; sizes="100vw"&#10; type="image/webp"&#10; /&gt;&#10; &#10; &lt;img&#10; width="800"&#10; height="400"&#10; class="mx-auto my-0 rounded-md"&#10; alt="Podcatcher"&#10; loading="lazy" decoding="async"&#10; &#10; src="https://hugovk.dev/blog/2011/symbian-platform-share-ii/ovid-podcatcher-201102-201105_hu_fa5182a58c958e8c.png" srcset="https://hugovk.dev/blog/2011/symbian-platform-share-ii/ovid-podcatcher-201102-201105_hu_fddad1a06aa80a15.png 330w,https://hugovk.dev/blog/2011/symbian-platform-share-ii/ovid-podcatcher-201102-201105_hu_fa5182a58c958e8c.png 660w&#10; &#10; ,https://hugovk.dev/blog/2011/symbian-platform-share-ii/ovid-podcatcher-201102-201105.png 800w&#10; &#10; &#10; ,https://hugovk.dev/blog/2011/symbian-platform-share-ii/ovid-podcatcher-201102-201105.png 800w&#10; "&#10; sizes="100vw"&#10; &#10; /&gt;&#10; &lt;/picture&gt;&#10; &#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;/figure&gt;&#10;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;(&lt;a href="https://web.archive.org/web/20110921195226/http://yfrog.com/h7enqep"&gt;source&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Podcatcher has a touch/non-touch ratio of around 8/2, and S^3 account for around 75% of&#10;downloads. I expect there&amp;rsquo;s so much Symbian^X because of the&#10;&lt;a href="https://web.archive.org/web/20110921195226/http://europe.nokia.com/support/product-support/podcasting"&gt;Nokia Podcasting&lt;/a&gt;&#10;application either pre-installed or available as a sisx for older S60 3.x phones.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;hr&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Now some charts with a nice long history: a pair of applications from&#10;&lt;a href="https://web.archive.org/web/20110921195226/http://www.ravensoft.co.uk/"&gt;Ravensoft&lt;/a&gt; that&#10;have been in Ovi Store since June 2009.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Tweets60 with over 650,000 downloads (June 2009 - August 2011):&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;figure&gt;&#10; &#10; &#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10; &#10; &lt;picture&#10; class="mx-auto my-0 rounded-md"&#10; &#10; &gt;&#10; &#10; &#10; &#10; &#10; &lt;source&#10; &#10; srcset="https://hugovk.dev/blog/2011/symbian-platform-share-ii/ovid-tweets60-200906-201108_hu_c7058c8df2f49859.webp 330w,https://hugovk.dev/blog/2011/symbian-platform-share-ii/ovid-tweets60-200906-201108_hu_a5f898a987d3c5d.webp 660w&#10; &#10; &#10; ,https://hugovk.dev/blog/2011/symbian-platform-share-ii/ovid-tweets60-200906-201108_hu_e2a94732b66070e1.webp 720w&#10; &#10; &#10; &#10; &#10; ,https://hugovk.dev/blog/2011/symbian-platform-share-ii/ovid-tweets60-200906-201108_hu_e2a94732b66070e1.webp 720w&#10; &#10; "&#10; &#10; sizes="100vw"&#10; type="image/webp"&#10; /&gt;&#10; &#10; &lt;img&#10; width="720"&#10; height="450"&#10; class="mx-auto my-0 rounded-md"&#10; alt="Tweets60"&#10; loading="lazy" decoding="async"&#10; &#10; src="https://hugovk.dev/blog/2011/symbian-platform-share-ii/ovid-tweets60-200906-201108_hu_6f32bc7b193611b6.jpg" srcset="https://hugovk.dev/blog/2011/symbian-platform-share-ii/ovid-tweets60-200906-201108_hu_8da426fdb919c604.jpg 330w,https://hugovk.dev/blog/2011/symbian-platform-share-ii/ovid-tweets60-200906-201108_hu_6f32bc7b193611b6.jpg 660w&#10; &#10; ,https://hugovk.dev/blog/2011/symbian-platform-share-ii/ovid-tweets60-200906-201108.jpg 720w&#10; &#10; &#10; ,https://hugovk.dev/blog/2011/symbian-platform-share-ii/ovid-tweets60-200906-201108.jpg 720w&#10; "&#10; sizes="100vw"&#10; &#10; /&gt;&#10; &lt;/picture&gt;&#10; &#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;/figure&gt;&#10;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;(&lt;a href="https://web.archive.org/web/20110921195226/http://www.facebook.com/photo.php?pid=611731&amp;amp;l=6a4561a69f&amp;amp;id=134860453217403"&gt;source&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Tweets60 is better on non-touchscreen, so has a bias towards S60 3rd edition devices,&#10;and the touch/non-touch ratio is about 1/1.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;hr&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Finally, Ravensoft&amp;rsquo;s&#10;&lt;a href="https://www.facebook.com/BatteryExtender/photos"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Battery Extender&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; with 2.5m&#10;downloads (June 2009 - May 2011):&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;figure&gt;&#10; &#10; &#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10; &#10; &lt;picture&#10; class="mx-auto my-0 rounded-md"&#10; &#10; &gt;&#10; &#10; &#10; &#10; &#10; &lt;source&#10; &#10; srcset="https://hugovk.dev/blog/2011/symbian-platform-share-ii/ovid-batteryextender-200906-2011045_hu_6c06273422c10392.webp 330w,https://hugovk.dev/blog/2011/symbian-platform-share-ii/ovid-batteryextender-200906-2011045_hu_823c3c334d17d3e3.webp 660w&#10; &#10; ,https://hugovk.dev/blog/2011/symbian-platform-share-ii/ovid-batteryextender-200906-2011045_hu_9af44da042fb7d55.webp 1024w&#10; &#10; &#10; ,https://hugovk.dev/blog/2011/symbian-platform-share-ii/ovid-batteryextender-200906-2011045_hu_62df1d1d1d7c9211.webp 1320w&#10; "&#10; &#10; sizes="100vw"&#10; type="image/webp"&#10; /&gt;&#10; &#10; &lt;img&#10; width="1920"&#10; height="1200"&#10; class="mx-auto my-0 rounded-md"&#10; alt="Battery Extender"&#10; loading="lazy" decoding="async"&#10; &#10; src="https://hugovk.dev/blog/2011/symbian-platform-share-ii/ovid-batteryextender-200906-2011045_hu_907b1165c68a1e79.png" srcset="https://hugovk.dev/blog/2011/symbian-platform-share-ii/ovid-batteryextender-200906-2011045_hu_bbfa7cdc05fdbafc.png 330w,https://hugovk.dev/blog/2011/symbian-platform-share-ii/ovid-batteryextender-200906-2011045_hu_907b1165c68a1e79.png 660w&#10; &#10; ,https://hugovk.dev/blog/2011/symbian-platform-share-ii/ovid-batteryextender-200906-2011045_hu_e9beae6378b997d.png 1024w&#10; &#10; &#10; ,https://hugovk.dev/blog/2011/symbian-platform-share-ii/ovid-batteryextender-200906-2011045_hu_6d2c9c5b6621b91d.png 1320w&#10; "&#10; sizes="100vw"&#10; &#10; /&gt;&#10; &lt;/picture&gt;&#10; &#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;/figure&gt;&#10;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;(&lt;a href="https://www.flickr.com/photos/andynugent/5736310405/"&gt;source&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;This is probably a fairly good representation as it appeals to all handsets. The&#10;touch/non-touch ratio is around 6/4.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="../symbian-platform-share"&gt;Click here&lt;/a&gt; to find out how to use Ovid; if any other&#10;developers/publishers have run the scripts, leave a comment! Thanks to&#10;&lt;a href="https://web.archive.org/web/20180306200409/https://twitter.com/nugent"&gt;Andy Nugent&lt;/a&gt;&#10;from&#10;&lt;a href="https://web.archive.org/web/20110921195226/http://www.developer.nokia.com/Community/Blogs/blog/hugo-van-kemenades-forum-nokia-blog/2011/09/08/symbian-platform-share-in-the-ovi-store-ii#:~:text=Nugent%C2%A0from-,Ravensoft,-and%C2%A0Sebastian"&gt;Ravensoft&lt;/a&gt;&#10;and&#10;&lt;a href="https://web.archive.org/web/20110921195226/http://twitter.com/teknolog"&gt;Sebastian Brannstrom&lt;/a&gt;&#10;for sharing their charts.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;hr&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Originally posted on&#10;&lt;a href="https://web.archive.org/web/20110921195226/http://www.developer.nokia.com/Community/Blogs/blog/hugo-van-kemenades-forum-nokia-blog/2011/09/08/symbian-platform-share-in-the-ovi-store-ii"&gt;Hugo van Kemenade&amp;rsquo;s Forum Nokia Blog&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;</description></item></channel></rss>